# Keep generated artifacts byte-preserving: no line-ending normalization or textconv.
# The internal scripts/check-wireguard-core-drift.sh rebuild verifies byte identity.
# The QA-enablement scan excludes only the three compiled Rust archives; its --text
# diff still scans headers, plist, toolchain metadata and unexpected files in build/.
#
# Deliberately OUTSIDE build/. Living inside it made this file unverifiable: it is
# hand-maintained, so the rebuild preserved it byte-for-byte and it matched in both drift
# manifests; it sat beside generated artifacts without its own provenance check; and its own `* binary`
# rule matched itself, so even an ordinary `git diff` of it was opaque. A file that governs
# how the artifacts are stored should not be one of the things the artifact gate cannot see.
build/** binary
